---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Perforated Metal Sheet — Specs, Prices & Anping Factories" description="Perforated metal sheets for filtration, architecture, and industrial use. Round, square, and slotted holes. Materials, thickness, and direct factory sourcing from Anping, China.">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 flex flex-col lg:flex-row gap-8">
    <!-- Main Content -->
    <article class="flex-1 min-w-0 prose">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-theme-primary">Perforated Metal Sheet</h1>
      <p class="text-theme-secondary">Perforated metal is sheet metal punched with precise hole patterns. Anping factories produce it for filtration, screening, architectural façades, acoustic panels, machine guards, and decorative applications in steel, stainless steel, aluminum, and specialty alloys.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">Materials</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Material</th><th>Common Grades</th><th>Thickness</th><th>Best For</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Low-carbon steel</td><td>Q235, SPCC</td><td>0.5–6.0mm</td><td>General industrial, filters</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Galvanized steel</td><td>DX51D, SGCC</td><td>0.5–3.0mm</td><td>Outdoor, corrosion-resistant</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Stainless steel</td><td>304, 316, 430</td><td>0.3–5.0mm</td><td>Food, chemical, pharmaceutical</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Aluminum</td><td>1060, 3003, 5052</td><td>0.3–4.0mm</td><td>Architectural, lightweight</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Copper / brass</td><td>C11000, H62, H65</td><td>0.3–2.0mm</td><td>Decorative, acoustic, EMI</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">Common specifications</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Hole Shape</th><th>Hole Diameter (mm)</th><th>Pitch (mm)</th><th>Thickness (mm)</th><th>Open Area %</th><th>Application</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Round staggered</td><td>0.8–25.4</td><td>1.5–35</td><td>0.3–3.0</td><td>20–70%</td><td>Filtration, screening</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Round straight</td><td>1.0–30</td><td>2.0–40</td><td>0.5–4.0</td><td>15–60%</td><td>Grilles, vents</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Square</td><td>2×2–50×50</td><td>3–60</td><td>0.5–4.0</td><td>20–65%</td><td>Partitions, ceilings</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Slotted</td><td>0.8×10–5×50</td><td>2–60</td><td>0.5–4.0</td><td>15–55%</td><td>Sieves, dryers</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Hexagonal</td><td>3–25</td><td>4–35</td><td>0.5–3.0</td><td>30–75%</td><td>Architectural, acoustic</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">Standard sheet sizes: 1000×2000mm, 1220×2440mm, 1250×2500mm, 1500×3000mm. Custom sizes available. <a href="/tools/woven-wire-mesh-weight-calculator/" class="text-theme-accent">Estimate weight →</a></p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">What to specify when ordering</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Material and grade (e.g., SS304, 3003 aluminum, Q235)</li>
        <li>Hole shape, diameter, and pattern (staggered or straight)</li>
        <li>Sheet thickness and dimensions</li>
        <li>Open area percentage or porosity requirement</li>
        <li>Surface finish: mill finish, polished, powder coated, anodized</li>
        <li>Edge margins: standard margins or custom</li>
        <li>Quantity in m² or sheets</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">Price reference</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-4">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th class="text-left p-3 border border-theme bg-theme-tertiary font-semibold text-theme-primary">Product</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3 border border-theme bg-theme-tertiary font-semibold text-theme-primary">Spec</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3 border border-theme bg-theme-tertiary font-semibold text-theme-primary">Price Range (USD/m²)</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3 border border-theme bg-theme-tertiary font-semibold text-theme-primary">MOQ</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3 border border-theme bg-theme-tertiary font-semibold text-theme-primary">Lead Time</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Mild steel perforated</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Round 3mm hole, 5mm pitch, 1.0mm thick</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">$12–22/m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">50 m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">10–15 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Galvanized perforated</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Round 5mm hole, 8mm pitch, 1.0mm thick</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">$15–28/m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">50 m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">12–18 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">SS304 perforated</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Round 2mm hole, 4mm pitch, 1.0mm thick</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">$30–55/m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">30 m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">15–25 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Aluminum perforated</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Round 3mm hole, 5mm pitch, 1.0mm thick</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">$25–45/m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">50 m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">15–22 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Architectural custom</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Custom pattern, powder coated</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">$45–120/m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">20 m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">25–40 days</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-theme-muted mb-6">*Indicative 2025–2026 ranges. Actual pricing depends on material cost, hole complexity, tooling setup, order volume, and surface finish. Always request formal quotes.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">FAQ</h2>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">What's the difference between staggered and straight hole patterns?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Staggered: holes offset in alternating rows, maximum open area and strength. Most common for filtration and screening. Straight: holes aligned in rows and columns, cleaner look for architectural and decorative use. Staggered is usually cheaper to produce.</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">What open area percentage should I choose?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Higher open area = better flow but less strength. Filtration: 30–50%. Speaker grilles: 40–60%. Acoustic panels: 50–70%. Architectural sunscreens: 30–50%. Safety guards: 20–40% for strength.</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">Can I get custom hole patterns or logos?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Yes. CNC punching and laser cutting allow custom patterns, images, and logos. Tooling cost applies for unique punch shapes. Minimum order for custom tooling is usually higher (100+ m²). Architectural projects often use custom patterns.</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">How do I calculate open area for round holes?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">For staggered round holes: Open area ≈ 0.905 × (d/t)² × 100%, where d = hole diameter, t = pitch (center-to-center spacing). Example: 3mm holes on 5mm pitch = 0.905 × (3/5)² = 32.6% open area.</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">What's the minimum thickness for perforated metal?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Down to 0.3mm for stainless and aluminum with laser cutting. Standard punching handles 0.5–6.0mm. Thinner sheets are more prone to warping and need careful handling. For structural use, 1.5mm+ is recommended.</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">Can perforated sheets be bent, rolled, or welded?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Yes. Perforated sheets can be brake-formed, rolled into cylinders, and welded. Note: welding near holes may cause distortion. For cylindrical filters, specify whether sheet should be pre-rolled or rolled after perforating. Powder coating after fabrication is common.</p>
      </details>

      <div class="not-prose mt-8 bg-theme-secondary text-white rounded-xl p-6">
        <p class="font-semibold text-lg">Get quotes from Anping perforated metal factories</p>
        <a href="/inquiry/" class="inline-block mt-3 accent-bg hover:accent-bg font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg transition-colors">Send an inquiry →</a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Sidebar -->
    <aside class="lg:w-80 shrink-0">
      <div class="sticky top-24 space-y-6">
        <!-- Quick Tools -->
        <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-lg p-5">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-theme-accent tracking-widest mb-3">QUICK TOOLS</p>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-theme-primary mb-3">Calculate & Convert</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
            <li>
